    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "5-FU 5% cream 2 times a day for 3 to 4 weeks; it inhibits thymidylate synthetase and was the most effective of four field treatments in one trial; adding calcipotriol 0.005% may enhance it"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Alternatives: diclofenac 3% gel 2 times a day for 60 to 90 days (low efficacy); tirbanibulin 1% ointment once a day for 5 days (limited data)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Redness, scaling and pain during treatment and usually for 1 to 2 weeks after. Photodynamic therapy (aminolevulinate or methyl aminolevulinate plus light) is another field option"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
